  message: "Static code evidence as of 2026-04-17 dev @ commit 3c9bcc7c9 (refactor: shared has_concept/get_concept helpers):\n\nAudit of every consumer of symbol.meta['concepts']:\n1. packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/middleware_chain.py:82 — uses has_concept(sym, 'middleware') — correct\n2. packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/_concept_utils.py — defines has_concept + get_concept helpers with isinstance(c, dict) guards — correct\n3. packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ranking.py:632 — isinstance(concept, dict) and concept.get('concept') in _LOGGING_CONCEPTS — correct\n4. packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/framework_patterns.py:986 — if not isinstance(concept, dict): continue; concept.get('concept') == concept_name — correct\n5. framework_patterns.py:1270 — concept.get('concept') == 'route' (inside the emitter, which controls the shape — safe) — correct\n6. framework_patterns.py:1281 — concept.get('concept') (inside emitter) — correct\n7. All other Framework-subcategory linkers (orm.py, subprocess_cli.py, http.py, openapi.py) migrated to has_concept/get_concept helpers per the 3c9bcc7c9 refactor — correct\n\nNo surviving list[str] membership test. The original audit report (concept_tag_audit_04172026_0335.md) called out the middleware_chain.py:82 violation; it is now resolved.\n\nBakeoff validation of middleware-chain-edge emission in production is a separate concern (dynamic invariant, not this static one) — the current invariant's statement is about consumer shape, which is now uniformly correct."  # b78d
